# Barge-in (checkpoint interruption): a streamed reply plays one
# sentence-chunk at a time, and playback_thread briefly unmutes the
# recorder in the gap between chunks — never mid-sentence — to check
# whether the caller has started talking again. Genuine speech during
# that gap sets this Event; playback_thread reads it, abandons the rest
# of the current reply, and lets the recorder keep listening instead of
# re-muting. Set only by recorder_thread, cleared and read only by
# playback_thread — single writer/single reader, no lock needed (same
# reasoning already used for _call_gen elsewhere in this file).
_caller_speaking = threading.Event()

# The reply_id of a reply that was abandoned mid-stream via barge-in.
# Written only by playback_thread (when it detects the interruption),
# read only by processor_thread (to stop generating/synthesizing more
# sentences for a reply nobody is going to hear). Deliberately never
# reset back to None — reply_id is a monotonically increasing counter,
# so a stale value can never accidentally match a future reply; trying
# to clear it at "the right moment" would risk a late-arriving stale
# chunk from the SAME abandoned reply slipping past the check instead.
_abandoned_reply_id = None

